      "text": [
        " - «مَنْ صَلَّى فِي اَلْمَسْجِدِ اَلْحَرَامِ صَلاَةً مَكْتُوبَةً قَبِلَ اَللَّهُ بِهَا مِنْهُ كُلَّ صَلاَةٍ صَلاَّهَا مُنْذُ يَوْمَ وَجَبَتْ عَلَيْهِ اَلصَّلاَةُ وَ كُلَّ صَلاَةٍ يُصَلِّيهَا إِلَى أَنْ يَمُوتَ»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.681 - Abu Hamza al-Thumali narrated from Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as) that He said:\n\"Whoever performs an obligatory prayer in the Sacred Mosque (Masjid al-Haram), Allah (swt) accepts it as equivalent to every prayer they have performed since the day prayer became obligatory upon them, and every prayer they will perform until they die.\""
        ]
      }
